+// ===[ Buffers shared between geometries (gl3Caps.sharedBuffers) ]===
+// A geometry with a vertex and an index buffer of its own means other buffers for every
+// atomic drawn. Here geometries of one vertex format lie side by side in a page: a vertex
+// buffer for pageVertices vertices, an index buffer, and one vertex array object for all of
+// them. A geometry's indices are moved up by where its vertices begin in the page, and its
+// meshes are drawn from where its indices begin. Free room is kept as two lists of extents,
+// in order and joined where they touch; a page nobody uses is deleted.
+// A geometry whose vertices change (it is instanced again: water) leaves for buffers of its
+// own, since changing part of a buffer makes ANGLE hand the whole of it to Direct3D again.
+
+struct Extent
+{
+	uint32 start, count;
